Step 4: Publish the website
WordPress is arguably the best content management system for bloggers, entrepreneurs, and small business owners with no technical background whatsoever. With the help of plugins, themes, and a user-friendly dashboard, anyone can build the site of their dreams without ever touching code.
If you’re like me who constantly fiddle around the components of the platforms I use, then you’ll encounter the dreaded “white screen of death” — at least once during your time with WordPress.
This is more likely to occur on websites that push their resource allocation with fancy visuals, rich content, and plugins. One example is an e-commerce site, which consumes a ton of data and memory to operate.
Once you arrive at your hosting account’s cPanel login page, go ahead and provide your credentials.
Upon logging in, you should see a screen with sections for your web server’s files, domains, software and so on. Look for the ‘File Manager’ icon to proceed.
In the root folder of your WordPress site, look for a file called ‘wp-config.php.' This is where you can manually increase the size of your PHP memory limit.
To modify the PHP memory limit, you just need to paste a short line of code:
That said, the code above instructs WordPress to raise the PHP memory limit to 256 MB, which should be more than enough to ensure the normal operation of most websites — even for online stores. Newly-added codes should be highlighted in blue.
If a plugin causes your PHP memory exhaustion issue, then you should be able to log in to your WordPress dashboard again.
Now, head back to your file manager and revert the ‘plugins.old’ folder name into ‘plugins’. Refresh your WordPress dashboard to re-scan all the system folders.
Reverting to the Default Theme Lastly, if you suspect that the PHP memory exhaustion error is caused by a new theme, then you can resolve it by reverting to the default theme.
Take note that renaming the folder wouldn’t work because WordPress will still detect the theme files. But if you delete the theme’s folder, WordPress will be forced to revert to the default theme.
Here is another useful post that can help you fix some issues with this content management system. Good luck and have fun learning!
HRANK is a site that offers information on web hosting companies. It has a fairly large number of reviews along with a transparent methodology and something that most review sites don’t offer – comprehensive data on web hosting company uptime and performance.
We’re not talking about helping one or two small businesses here – we’re talking about them helping literally hundreds of companies with the SEO and hosting needs. As they say, the best way to learn is through experience.
HRANK is Turning Data into Helpful Information
Because of the sites they helped manage and the sheer spread of hosting companies they worked with, HRANK found themselves with a massive amount of data. This inspired them to do what all geeks do with it – turn meaningless data into valuable information.
Our goal is simple; To bring some transparency to the web hosting market and show people the facts on the ground. – Victor Kluchenia, Co-Founder, HRANK
“It is exciting for us to create something new and useful in this market that no one has done before. Having faced so many challenges in the past seeking the best hosting to go for, we know that the information will help others out as well,” says Victor.
Once all that data is in, they reviewed each one of those companies and threw in their own thoughts as well. The result was a unique HRANK Score which according to Victor is currently something that’s quite unique to the industry.
The data recording carried out by HRANK commenced in June 2018 and has been ongoing since then. At this point of time, they are monitoring over 40,000 shared IP addresses from more than 300 service providers.
Although HRANK does earn money from affiliate programs, Victor is adamant that that isn’t what motivates the team. His opinion is that their journey towards success will be based on offering users a truly useful product, perseverance, transparency and a real interest in the industry.
This means that the general public, which is anyone who needs help, has a free source of reliable information to come to for information about choosing a web host. Imagine the cost and trouble that could save for so many newbies to the game!
Still, the objective is clear to Victor; to be the service that people come to for web hosting evaluation and to help them compare and select the best for their own website. About Timothy Shim
