44 Ways to Become an Authority in Your Niche | WHSR
Home › Blog › Blogging Tips › 44 Ways to Become an Authority in Your Niche
Want to become an authority in your blog's niche?
TrustConsumers purchase from bloggers they trust, even if they don’t know them. In 2012, Neilsen conducted a study showing that 92% of consumers trusted recommendations from individuals over brands.
Earn an AdvanceBloggers and ebook writers are offered publishing house contracts. For example, Angela England got offered a contract based on her prior through her blog and work with others.
Speaking FeesBloggers with authority can easily pitch to speak at a conference, especially if you have connections. My first gig was speaking about SEO at iRetreat.
Speak at new, small venues in your niche. Use Blab, Facebook Live or Periscope to build your speaking skills and portfolio.
Champion others. When you have common ground with big leaders or small bloggers, support their causes with tags, shout outs, posts, shares, and promotions.
Charge what you’re worth. Influencers with authority share good advice but never work for free.
Credit your inspiration publicly. When you are inspired, go ahead and let that influencer know by tagging on social media and thanking him.
Continually to improve yourself and learn your topic. There’s nothing worse than seeing a recent post with outdated information.
Do your research and check your answer, but don’t answer what you don’t know. Instead, reach out to others for answers you need.
Help bloggers behind you. Know someone up and coming in your niche?
The one thing most thought leaders have in common is respect for others, even their detractors. Stay classy in all your dealings.
Avoid hot button topics outside of your niche. Be yourself and be authentic, but jumping on debates that are full of vitriol doesn’t look professional even if you are trying to be the “voice of reason.”
Fellow blogger unfairly smeared?
Speak up and help your fellow man.
Connect with people who have the problem you had and solved. They’ll want to know that and may even purchase from you, but you must first build rapport.
Answer the questions no one else is answering. Many years ago, I had a viral post on how to shift your blog from Movable Type to WordPress because no one had the answer.
It could be your age, location, how you do it, where you started from, your income, etc. Make serving others your mission.
If something doesn’t feel right, turn it down. You will never feel right about it if you don’t.
Promote things you believe in. After turning down that project, I pitched brands I liked for the same rate.
Too many bloggers think they are too small or not experienced enough. Build your reputation and experience on your own.
Use these 44 ways to build authority in your niche and you can become a better blogger.
