You just want your site to be restored as quickly as possible in case of security breaches. That’s why UpdraftPlus’ interface is so simple – it only has three main buttons: “Backup Now,” “Restore,” and “Clone/Migrate.”
When it comes to the clone/migration feature, just remember that you need UpdraftMigrator – a paid tool that allows you to move your WordPress site to a new address. However, this feature isn’t helpful for beginners, so you should stick to the free backup plugin for now.
Sure, you can always approve or delete comments through the built-in commenting system, but going the manual route can take a tremendous amount of time. Take note that you also have to identify and respond to legitimate comments if you want to establish a more approachable brand.
Whether you like it or not, search engine optimization (SEO) is essential for the growth of your website.93% of online experiences start with a simple online search– So if you want the online audience to discover your site, ranking highly in search engine rankings is a must.
Yoast SEO integrates directly to the built-in post and page editor to review the searchability of your content in real time. It works by analyzing on-page SEO factors such as subheadings, paragraph length, keyword density, and the content’s meta description.
To activate Live Composer, go to Pages > All Pages, choose a page you want to edit, and then click “Edit in Live Composer.” This will load the chosen page and bring up the Live Composer interface. To add new elements or “modules” on your page, just click and drag an icon from the main toolbar.
For many years, Contact Form 7 has been the go-to WordPress plugin when it comes to creating contact forms. It is a simple tool that allows you to create fully-functional contact forms within minutes.
Regardless if you have an online portfolio, photography blog, or online store, you need images to boost your site’s engagement factor. Unfortunately, a lot of beginners make the mistake of using images that are needlessly large.
WP Smush can also be set to optimize new images on upload automatically. Just scroll down to the settings section and check “Automatically smush my images on upload.” Once activated, you never have to worry about images slowing down your site again.
Shortcodes Ultimate allows you to use a wide range of shortcodes that can spice up your WordPress website. All you need to do is to copy-paste shortcodes to implement elements such as galleries, multiple content tabs, quotes, and frames.
With plugins like Live Composer, Shortcodes Ultimate, and Contact Form 7, you have everything you need to customize the content area. With WooSidebars, you can now have complete control over everything on your WordPress website.
To use your new widget area, make sure to choose a sidebar to replace from the drop-down menu on the right. Also, don’t forget to set the appropriate conditions on when and where the sidebar will appear.
On Your Search for More Must-Have WP Plugins…
Just remember to be cautious when installing plugins, especially if they’re coming from third-party sources. Don’t rely on the publisher’s words and look for legitimate reviews.
We talked about SEO and marketing until midnight and my head is still high on all the good topics that came up from the discussion.
Let's see them all, one by one.
“We could exchange links, find partners,” said one of my friends, “Or can you write a post on your blog to help our client?”.
I told my friends that the new Google is about earning links, not building them. They looked back at me in bewilderment.
If you want to build relationships with other webmasters through link exchange, don't do it for SEO.
Are there link building methods that still work for SEO?
The Broken Link Building Method — Find great content, check the on-page links and, if you find any broken links, get in touch with the webmaster to suggest a great resource to replace that link (maybe yours?).
Email Outreach — Could your content really help someone else's users?
Neil Patel's Guide to Email Outreach is your friend.
Some old, good socials don't exist anymore or have been replaced by different services, and the new ones may be gone tomorrow, too.
One idea is to not focus on a single solution. Whether you choose to work with mainstream social, little known social networks or a mix of those, don't just use Facebook or Twitter or Google+.
Most of all, be friendly and helpful, because when a social network closes down, people will still remember you for who you are— and they will follow you elsewhere.
“Our client can't get to place their site in Google,” one of my friends said (and reiterated recently), “What to do?”
My friend's client may use better website copy and good calls to action to motivate prospective buyers, but since the business is of a kind (artistic furniture) where you don't need a lot of copy, it won't work unless you play it smart… and that's not easy.
How can this business market without Google?
Funny furniture geared for happy lovers of fun-looking furniture makes good material for funny videos. A certain, little-known technique for designing custom furniture may be what you need to produce an educational video or a webinar.
Websites, yellow pages, magazines and blogs. The right places, where you know your target audience spends most of her online time.
Our Jerry Low recently published an enlightening post at TwelveSkip on how to grow your blog traffic without Google. If you're like my friends' client, you may want to read it (even if you don't have a blog).
But, you can get creative with sponsorships!
You can give a special discount on your services to current customers who are willing to promote you. — Fair exchange, after all.
Do you only optimize for Google or do you try to distribute your eggs in more baskets?
