The different types of applications for which synchronous motors are used can be classified as:
Just by visual inspection, you can know if a machine is a synchronous or an induction motor. A synchronous motor is a doubly excited motor, which means it needs both field and armature excitation.
If there is a field connection, then the motor is synchronous (assuming it can’t be a dc motor). Induction motor does not have any field connections but only stator supply.
They require some external rotating mechanism to bring their speed close to synchronous speed to before they get synchronized.
These motors are not self-starting motors because they need some external rotating system for its starting and synchronizing.
